## What was adapted, and where

| From | Adapted in | What carried over |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `imessage-agent-template/src/lib/redact.ts` | `giwacard/src/mcp/redact.ts` | The two-layer redaction shape: a field-name denylist plus a regex backstop over serialized output. The threat is inverted — that template keeps a card *number* out of a model's context; ours keeps out the *key that spends the card*. |
| `agent-card-skill/SKILL.md` | `giwacard/skill/SKILL.md` | Document structure: vocabulary, workflows, safety rules, error table. Content is rewritten for the onchain model; the fiat-specific material (KYC, Visa, custodial balances, US billing addresses) does not apply here and was dropped. |
| `@agent-cards/mcp` tool surface | `giwacard/src/mcp/tools/` | The shape of an MCP tool surface for spend authorization, and the asynchronous approval pattern where an over-policy request returns an id the agent polls later. Migrated to MCP SDK v2. |
| `agentcard-mcp` packaging docs | `giwacard/llms-install.md` | The idea of a machine-executable install runbook aimed at a coding agent rather than a human reader. |

Third-party dependencies retain their own licences; see each package's
